From d9d821ceb069e96d94b24e426f43060bb69b674a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:10:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] COMPAT G5: model the ACPI PM block so the ICH9 lane boots

The --lpc=ich9 blocker was recorded as a POST reset loop at RIP 0xefa1f.
It was not: with the ICH9 LPC identity stock SeaBIOS builds ACPI, publishes
the RSDP and points its own timer at PMBASE+8 (TimerPort=0xb008).  The
emulated chipset had no ACPI PM block, so that port read 0xFFFFFFFF forever
and no timer_check() deadline could expire.  The visible stall is the AHCI
probe waiting for DET==3 on an empty port (PxSSTS 0x1a8) while port 0 is
accepted (0x123); the 718-instruction loop around f0068 with 'in eax,dx' at
f010b is the wait, not the cause.

src/pm.{h,c} model the 0x40-byte ACPI PM register block: PMBASE (default
0xB000, bits 15:7 of LPC config 0x40..0x43 applied through the LPC cfg_write
hook) and a 24-bit read-only TMR at +8 counting three counts per PIT tick
(3.579545 MHz vs 1.193182 MHz = one count per 128 retired instructions,
remainder carried).  Every other byte reads zero and writes are swallowed;
ports outside the window still float high.  pm_init() runs in
devices_init_common next to the PIT.

Measured on the G3 accepted image with the unmodified Debian SeaBIOS
1.16.3-2: [kernel] shell active; kmain idling., executed_steps=829920364,
fault=0, RC 0 in 158 s; the marker first appears between 435M and 445M
instructions.  boot_info_t now carries rsdp_phys=0xf6830 and eight E820
entries; a post-marker snapshot walks RSDP 0xf6830 -> RSDT 0x7ffe3a0 with
four checksum-valid tables (FACP, SSDT, APIC/MADT, MCFG) whose I/O APIC
entry 0xfec00000 matches the guest's '(MADT agree)' line.

The E820 7-vs-8 question closes with the same fix: the eighth entry
0xfed1c000+0x4000 is the ICH9 RCRB that SeaBIOS reserves only on the ICH9
path.  QEMU's q35 map with the same ROM has the identical eight-entry shape;
the only numeric difference left is the firmware ACPI/NVS slab size
(16 KiB vs 132 KiB), both ending at 0x08000000.

Recorded, not fixed (guest side): AuraLite-OS madt_walk() accepts a type-2
ISO entry only when elen >= 12, while the ACPI structure is 10 bytes, so the
kernel prints 'overrides: none in the MADT' despite four ISOs; QEMU prints
the same line with the same BIOS.

Tests: tests/test_pm.c (6 vectors, in make test-unit; src/pm.c is linked
wherever src/pit.c is), make test-g5 (58 bundle checks, in make test),
make test-g5-nc (four tampered bundles), make test-g5-live (the frozen-timer
replay: no [BL3] in 300M vs 297585739 for the fixed tree).

Docs: docs/evidence/compat-g5/ (README, receipt, ACPI receipt, boot info,
bisect, negative control, inputs, commands), PROJECT_ANALYSIS 25 patches,
STATUS/COMPAT_PLAN/CHANGELOG/ROADMAP mark G5 delivered.
